==Restrictions==
Max # of Deployable Cats: 10

==Battleground==
{{EnemiesAppearing|Gory|Gory Dark|Angelic Gory|General GreGory}}
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn, delay 30~40 seconds<sup>900f~1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Gory|Gories]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*2 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*10 [[Gory|Gories]] spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*2 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 83.33 seconds<sup>2,500f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Gory Dark]] spawns.
**1 [[General GreGory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This can be a difficult stage due to the Cat deploy limit and how the enemies spawn on a timer. Cats with area attacks such as [[Paris Cat]], [[Drama Cats]], and [[Castaway Cat]] or melee cats such as [[Ring Girl Cat]], [[Butterfly Cat]], or [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]], if you have him, can fend off the various Gories. The trick is to not spam meatshields in the middle of the battle since they can clog up the limit and leave you with less offense which can result in you being overwhelmed. Eventually the Gories will trickle out leaving you with only infinite basic Gories who are easy to kill.

